# One account, least privilege.
#
# The broker credential is shared by the ingester (which subscribes) and the
# simulators - the software one and any physical ESP32 node, which is the whole
# point of the hardware seam. What nothing else needs is write access anywhere
# else or read access to anything: without an ACL, any process holding the
# credential - every container on the compose network, anything on the host's
# loopback - could publish readings indistinguishable from a real building's,
# and injected load flows straight into forecasts, anomalies and annual_kwh.
#
# $SYS/# is read-only and exists for the container healthcheck, which subscribes
# to it to prove the broker answers.

user gemp

topic readwrite gemp/reading/#
topic read $SYS/#
